etkutatásáról eddig beszámoltak. A szerkezet- \nvizsgálat azonban minden részletében még nincs \nlezárva, amint ezt láthatjuk Horii és mtsai [28] \nalábbi eredményeiből (6. ábra).\nAz eurocidint (39a, b) sósavas-etanollal (a)\nEzen eredmények alapján a kutatók [28] arra \nkövetkeztettek, hogy az eurocidin a (39a) és (39b) \nvariáns keverékéből áll és a 30-as gyűrűtagszámú \nmakro-lakton C—14 atomjához egy karboxil, \na C—15 és C—17-hez pedig egy-egy hidroxil-\n3 6 6\nX X X . \nÉ V F O L Y A M  \n7. \nS Z .--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStructures of maridomycins. (https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/saj/1/1/1_1_1/_pdf)\nciteturn10search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 18.9 years ago; Crawled: 18.9 years ago; Chemical structure diagram labeled “Structures of maridomycins.” ... (1) Eurocidin\nStructures of maridomycins.\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nChemical structure diagram labeled “Structures of maridomycins.” Below the structure is a substitution table for Maridomycin I–VI with columns R1 and R2:\n- Maridomycin I: R1 = COCH2CH3, R2 = COCH2CH(CH3)2\n- II: R1 = COCH3, R2 = COCH2CH(CH3)2\n- III: R1 = COCH2CH3, R2 = COCH2CH3\n- IV: R1 = COCH3, R2 = COCH2CH3\n- V: R1 = COCH2CH3, R2 = COCH3\n- VI: R1 = COCH3, R2 = COCH3\n\nCaption: 図12. Maridomycin\n</visual_element>\n\n3. Antifungal substances  \n(1) Eurocidin\n\n上述したenteromycin生産菌 S. albireticuli No 3724 は菌体中に抗真菌性物質21) をつくった。菌体の MeOH抽出液を減圧下濃縮後、アルミナカラムに吸着させ w-BuOHで溶出し活性分画を集めて濃縮すると微細な針状晶が析出した。非常に特徴的なUV吸収を示し、広くかび類、酵母およびトリコモナス原虫などの生育を抑制したので eurocidin と名付けた。あとで判明したがこれは最初に分離された pentaene であった。\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProduction of tertiomycin (a new antibiotic substance), azomycin and eurocidin by S. eurocidicus (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/13286189/)\nciteturn10search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Production of tertiomycin (a new antibiotic substance), azomycin and eurocidin by S. eurocidicus\n\n. 1955 Aug;8(4):105-9.\n\n# Production of tertiomycin (a new antibiotic substance), azomycin and eurocidin by S. eurocidicus\n\nT OSATO, M UEDA, S FUKUYAMA, K YAGISHITA, Y OKAMI, H UMEZAWA\n\n  * PMID: 13286189\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\n# Production of tertiomycin (a new antibiotic substance), azomycin and eurocidin by S. eurocidicus\n\nT OSATO et al. J Antibiot (Tokyo). 1955 Aug.\n\n\n. 1955 Aug;8(4):105-9.\n\n### Authors\n\nT OSATO, M UEDA, S FUKUYAMA, K YAGISHITA, Y OKAMI, H UMEZAWA\n\n  * PMID: 13286189\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nCite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat [Select]\n\nNo abstract available\n\n## MeSH terms\n\n  * [Button: Anti-Bacterial Agents* ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Nitroimidazoles* ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Streptomyces* ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n## Substances\n\n  * [Button: Anti-Bacterial Agents ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Nitroimidazoles ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: azomycin ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMode of action of antibiotics I. Site of action of ascosin (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0006300261904504)\nciteturn10search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 65.1 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Ascosin, a heptaene antibiotic produced by Streptomyces canescus (NRRL 2419) which inhibited yeast respiration completely, had no effect on glycolysis.\n\n## Biochimica et Biophysica Acta\n\nVolume 53, Issue 2, 28 October 1961, Pages 391-396\n\n# Mode of action of antibiotics I. Site of action of ascosin\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1016/0006-3002(61)90450-4Get rights and content\n\n## Abstract\n\nAscosin, a heptaene antibiotic produced by Streptomyces canescus (NRRL 2419) which inhibited yeast respiration completely, had no effect on glycolysis. Ascosin did not inhibit the reduction of the dye, 2,6-dichlorophenol indophenol with succinate as the substrate. Nor did it inhibit the oxidation of reduced cytochrome c by yeast extracts. The reduction of 2,3,5-triphenyltetrazolium chloride, which accepts electrons from cytochrome a, was completely inhibited by ascosin when succinate was the substrate. Ascosin also inhibited the succinate → cytochrome c reductase system. Mixtures of ascosin and antimycin-A at low concentrations produced inhibition that was even greater than the sum of the individual inhibitions. From these data it is concluded that the site of action of ascosin is probably the same as that of antimycin A.\n\n\nAccess through your organization\n\n## References (10)\n\n  * M.M. Nachlas et al.\n\n### J. Biol. Chem.\n\n(1960)\n\n  * R.J. Hickey et al.\n\n### Antibiotics and Chemotherapy\n\n(1952)\n\n  * W.W. Umbreit et al.\n\n### Monometric Techniques\n\n(1957)\n\n  * K. Ahmad et al.\n\n### Arch. Biochem.\n\n(1950)\n\n  * M.B. Thorn\n\n### Biochem. J.\n\n(1956)\n\nThere are more references available in the full text version of this article.\n\n## Cited by (0)\n\nView full text\n\nCopyright © 1961 Published by Elsevier B.V.\n\n  * European Journal of Pharmacology, Volume 1005, 2025, Article 178080\n\nYa-qi Guo, …, Peng Li\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRhodomycin A (https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/9896436)\nciteturn10search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; # Rhodomycin A ...   * Rhodomycin A\nThe matching between the MeSH and compound records is performed by name matching (i.e., identical common names), as described in Kim et al., J. Cheminform., 2016, 8, 32.; Section reference: http://doi.org/10.1186/s13321-016-0142-6\n\n#### Depositor-Supplied Synonyms\n\n  * beta-Rhodomycin II\n  * RHODOMYCIN A\n  * NSC-136044\n  * 6E9E3X300A\n  * 23666-50-4\n  * 5,12-Naphthacenedione, 8-ethyl-7,8,9,10-tetrahydro-1,6,8,11-tetrahydroxy-7,10-bis((2,3,6-trideoxy-3-(dimethylamino)-alpha-L-lyxo-hexopyranosyl)oxy)-, (7R,8R,10S)-\n  * (7S,9R,10R)-7,10-bis[[(2S,4S,5S,6S)-4-(dimethylamino)-5-hydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl]oxy]-9-ethyl-4,6,9,11-tetrahydroxy-8,10-dihydro-7H-tetracene-5,12-dione\n  * DTXSID60417690\n  * (7S,9R,10R)-7,10-bis(((2S,4S,5S,6S)-4-(dimethylamino)-5-hydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl)oxy)-9-ethyl-4,6,9,11-tetrahydroxy-8,10-dihydro-7H-tetracene-5,12-dione\n  * RefChem:179296\n  * DTXCID101311106\n  * (7S,9R,10R)-7-((2R,4S,5S,6S)-4-(dimethylamino)-5-hydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl)oxy-10-((4S,5S,6S)-4-(dimethylamino)-5-hydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl)oxy-9-ethyl-4,6,9,11-tetrahydroxy-8,10-dihydro-7H-tetracene-5,12-dione\n  * Rhodomycin A [MI]\n  * UNII-6E9E3X300A\n  * .BETA.-RHODOMYCIN II\n  * RHODOMYCIN II, .BETA.\n  * orb3141722\n  * SCHEMBL30714406\n  * TN11322\n  * Q27264690\n  * 5,12-NAPHTHACENEDIONE, 8-ETHYL-7,8,9,10-TETRAHYDRO-1,6,8,11-TETRAHYDROXY-7,10-BIS((2,3,6-TRIDEOXY-3-(DIMETHYLAMINO)-.ALPHA.-L-LYXO-HEXOPYRANOSYL)OXY)-, (7R,8R,10S)-\n\nSource: PubChem; Context: Chemical names provided by individual data contributors. Synonyms of Substances corresponding to a PubChem Compound record are combined. Some contributed names may be considered erroneous and filtered out. The link on each synonym shows which depositors provided that particular synonym for this structure.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTHE JOURNAL OF ANTIBIOTICS — MAY 1990 (https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/antibiotics1968/43/5/43_5_462/_pdf)\nciteturn10search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.7 years ago; Crawled: 19.0 years ago; Eurocidin was found by Nakazawa7) as an anti-fungal antibiotic produced by S. albireticuli, and was designated as Eurocidin-T in this paper. ... Horii et al.8) reported the partial structure of Eurocidin-T as a pentaene containing eurocidins A and B, however the whole structure of any of eurocidins was still unknown.\nTHE JOURNAL OF ANTIBIOTICS — MAY 1990\n\nand C40H61NO14 for F-3, respectively.\n\nFrom the UV spectra, F-1, F-2 and F-3 were defined as the typical pentaene of polyene macrolide antibiotics. They were estimated as eurocidin-type compounds from producing microorganisms. Eurocidin was found by Nakazawa7) as an anti-fungal antibiotic produced by S. albireticuli, and was designated as Eurocidin-T in this paper. Eurocidin-T was a mixture of several related compounds. Horii et al.8) reported the partial structure of Eurocidin-T as a pentaene containing eurocidins A and B, however the whole structure of any of eurocidins was still unknown.\n\nEurocidin-T showed two major peaks and some minor peaks when it was subjected to HPLC (Fig. 5B). F-1, F-2 and F-3 isolated in this experiment were detected as almost a single peak (Fig. 5A shows the additive mixture of F-1, F-2 and F-3). The retention time of F-1 or F-2 was different from any component of Eurocidin-T, and only F-3 was eluted at similar retention time to that of one of the two major peaks of Eurocidin-T. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1973, 37(2):166. (https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=50ed71d1448e21754126502ecff8a5789a303ddf&repid=rep1&type=pdf)\nciteturn10search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Chemical composition ... Eurocidin A .......... ... Eurocidin B ... phenone that the problem of antibiotic identity\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDurhamycin, a Pentaene Antifungal Antibiotic from Streptomyces durhamensis sp. n (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1058409/)\nciteturn10search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Durhamycin, a Pentaene Antifungal Antibiotic from Streptomyces durhamensis sp. n ... Durhamycin, derived from a previously undescribed